   </description>
   <indicator measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">2. Project progress and achievement</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">In this section (maximum 1000 words), please

**For TMT+:**

Comment to what extent the outputs have been achieved. Comment on the activities that have taken place and the most important milestones.</narrative>
    </description>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2021-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2021-12-31"></period-end>
     <actual value="We are glad to report that almost all outputs, results and goals were achieved during this project.

Output 1 - we did not foresee that the INPFCA participants had no French language ability therefore they did not participate as hoped for. This is according to the organisation in Tunisia. The organisation was invited several times by the requesting organisation to participate. 

Output 2 - We developed a total of 6 modules. We see that in the logframe the numbers have been mixed up. It should have been 4 modules for Dairy technology and 2 for Entrepreneurship. All modules were developed in English and translated to French and one module was translated to Spanish and used in Colombia Nuffic project as well.The cooperation with all partners was excellent and very fruitful. The modules are visible in the Dairy Delta Academy platform. 

Output 3 - due to the extension we were able to conduct all F2F trainings starting in October 2021 through October 2022. The Entrepreneurship training was done in Octobre 2021 and in Octobre 2022. The milestone in this track was the workshop in Tunis (14th of July) in which all 3 TMT+ projects jointly presented their work and methodology. This was highly appreciated by all participants.

Output 4 - Both pilots were well done and conducted. The highlight or milestone of this output was the joint session of students working in the dairy pilot and with the staff lectures doing a pilot in Entrepreneurship. Both were finishing in the same week in the same place (October 2022), therefore we had the opportunity to have them share their experiences. To students were interviewed by the lecturers on how they felt about the Blended Learning platform, learning experience and more. This really was really helpful and encouraging for the lectures.

Within output 4 the only results not achieved was the practical distance learning program. It was to ambitious as well as to challenging for all partners to have to work in another language.

Output 5 - A powerful training and workshop was conducted in Tunis related social inclusion and gender issues. A mix of female and male participants were present and actively engaged."></actual>
    </period>
